{
  "$comment": [
    "Per-sprite export settings that cannot be derived from the sprite itself.",
    "",
    "RO gives a job three attack animations and a job really uses only one of them; which one is a",
    "property of the job rather than of the file, and nothing in the data says which. The same goes",
    "for a broken pose: plenty of sprites ship a `skill` that is one frame of nothing, and the fix a",
    "spriter reaches for is 'cast it on attack 3 instead'. Both are judgements somebody makes by",
    "looking at the sprite animate.",
    "",
    "They live here, checked in, so that judgement is made once. An export driven by this table",
    "reproduces the same art next month without anybody being told again - which is the whole",
    "difference between a pipeline and a person remembering. Without it, a re-export silently",
    "changes what the game draws.",
    "",
    "`attack` is which of attack/attack2/attack3 becomes the exported `attack`; it applies to the",
    "body AND every weapon in the same run, because a body swinging one pose against a weapon",
    "animated on another drifts apart frame by frame.",
    "",
    "`poses` remaps an exported name onto a different source pose. The name an engine asks for stays",
    "put; the frames behind it move. The manifest records the source as `base`, so an export always",
    "says which substitution it was made with.",
    "",
    "Match order: `keys` (a manifest key, most specific), then `names` (the sprite's own name), then",
    "`defaults` for the kind. Anything absent uses the defaults, which is nearly everything."
  ],
